## 2026-11-18 — Premium P29 complete
- Evidence ignite and camera focus per premium §8.3. The camera now skips the evidence framing when the user panned or zoomed since the last evidence change (set, switch, or clear), and the flag restarts at each change; clear still returns to fit unless the user moved. Clear fades veil, rims, and bloom from their current alpha while a switch's outgoing set keeps fading on its own clock (it was dropped at once), and a switch started during a clear fades the clearing set out. Same evidence on another wafer always draws settled (§8.7), even mid-ignite. Mobile (< 1024): any new evidence, from any trigger, scrolls the stage top to 8 px under the nav only when < 50 % of the stage is visible (store subscription in `LoadedLotOverview`, replacing the finding-only `onFindingToggle` scroll). The ignite then holds at t = 0 (`data-ignite-wait="true"`) until an IntersectionObserver sees >= 50 % or 400 ms pass. New pure helpers live in `linked-interactions.ts`: `computeStageVisibleRatio`, `shouldDeferEvidenceForStage`, and `navBarHeightPx`.
- Verified: typecheck and lint clean, `pnpm test` 339/339 (54 files; 3 new visibility tests, including a property test). After a fresh build, the new e2e `evidence-ignite-p29` passes 5/5: A38 (650 ms equals settled at < 1 % of disc pixels, 250 ms arc leads clockwise from 12 o'clock), the animated clear, the camera skip after a user zoom, mobile scroll then ignite, and reduced motion. `overlay-states-p8`, `loaded-responsive-p13`, `wafer-stage-r6`, `wafer-strip-p9`, `stats-p18`, `findings-p19`, `pareto-p20`, `yield-summary-p21`, `coach-marks-p25`, `stage-controls-p10`, `die-tiles-p6`, and `stage-shadows-p7` pass. `linked-interactions-r7` failed only its known 780 ms settle step (825 ms). No snapshot changes, no locale keys.
- Decisions (restrained): "Mobile" means below 1024, matching the existing §6.2 scroll gate, and visibility is measured under the nav. During the hold only the ignite waits. The camera flight starts at once, and an outgoing set stays frozen until the release. The strip dimming (0.32, `dur-2` `ease-out`) was already per spec and is unchanged.
